---
description: Prefer deterministic commands over hand-edits when reproducing known state
alwaysApply: true
---

# Commands Over Hand-Edits

- If a file's target state already exists at a git ref, restore it with `git checkout <ref> -- <path>` (or `git restore --source=<ref> -- <path>`). Do not reconstruct it via StrReplace/Write — you will leak formatting drift and waste tokens.
- Prefer known-correct commands (`git mv`, `git revert`, `git restore`, codemods, package-manager installs) over hand-editing whenever they produce the exact target state.
- Reserve manual edits for code that has no canonical source elsewhere.
